{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Let us journey and let us go, and I will go.</b> Since he mentioned two expressions, one in the plural and one in the singular, it is possible to say that he asked of him two things: he means, if you wish, let us journey and go together; or I will distance myself from you and go ahead, in the manner of (Genesis 21:16) ״ותשב לה מנגד הרחק״. And Jacob answered that it was impossible for him to go together with him, and that is what he said, 'My lord knows,' etc. But he went ahead of him — this one entered Seir and that one entered Sukkot." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'Let us journey and let us go' — Esav said to Jacob: let us divide this world and the world to come. Jacob said to him: 'the children are tender' — in commandments; and if I allocate them their portion in this world and press them one day into the day of judgment, all the flock will die — Israel, who are called flock — and they will not be able to endure the judgments of Gehinnom. 'Let my lord, I pray, pass before his servant' — let him take his portion first in this world, and I will conduct myself slowly; I will stand in my exile and lowliness, in the manner of (I Kings 21:27) ״ויהלך אט״, which is an expression of lowliness, meaning I will not stir up war nor grow strong in exile at all, but I will bear the yoke of subjugation — this is 'according to the pace of the work,' etc. And until when will the subjugation be? Until he comes, in the future, to Seir."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:26.035151695Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}